Language-neutral rules mechanics — MIT
======================================

Everything in this directory is covered by the MIT License in the top-level
`LICENSE` file, with no CC-BY-SA 4.0 carve-out.

These files carry no rulebook text: only slug identifiers, numbers, enums,
prerequisite and grant structures, and `source` citations recording the file and
line range each value was taken from. Where a slug echoes a rulebook term
(`spell.aegis_of_the_hearth`, `house.bjornaer`) it is used as an identifier, not
as expressive content.

The sibling `rules/i18n/` directory is different: its JSON form is MIT but the
rules text in its string values is CC-BY-SA 4.0. See `../i18n/LICENSE`.

Ars Magica is a trademark of Trident, Inc. d/b/a Atlas Games. This is an
unofficial fan tool, not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by Atlas
Games.

Project: https://github.com/garin1000/Ars-Magica-Character-Generator
